cm",35],[142207886,"Self Portrait with a Phrygian Cap",1792,0,0,null,5,"3/39/Self-Portrait_with_a_Phrygian_Cap_-_Girodet.jpg/330px-Self-Portrait_with_a_Phrygian_Cap_-_Girodet.jpg",0,0,1,0,59,"Autoportrait au bonnet phrygien | Self portrait in a Phrygian hat | Self-Portrait in a Phrygian Cap",null,"Gouache on ivory","Diameter 6 cm",42]],"summaryBase":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/","summaryLicence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","summaryKind":"excerpt","summaryLicenceUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/","factsSource":"Wikidata (CC0)","factsFormat":3,"rankVersion":1,"summaries":{"9401827":["The Burial of Atala or The Funeral of Atala is an 1808 oil-on-canvas painting by the French painter Anne-Louis Girodet de Roussy-Trioson. It depicts a scene from Francois-René de Chateaubriand's novel, Atala, written in 1801.","The Burial of Atala"],"17304998":["Pygmalion and Galatea is an oil-on-canvas painting by the French painter Anne-Louis Girodet. It represents the myth of Pygmalion and Galatea as told by Ovid in the Metamorphoses.","Pygmalion and Galatea (Girodet)"],"19521336":["Scene from a Deluge (Scène du déluge) is an oil-on-canvas painting by Anne-Louis Girodet. It was first exhibited at the Salon of 1806 and is now in the collection of the Louvre, in Paris.","Scene from a Deluge"],"19912314":["Portrait of Madame Reiset is an 1823 portrait painting by the French artist Anne-Louis Girodet de Roussy-Trioson. It depicts Colette-Désirée-Thérèse Godefroy (1782–1850), the wife of Jacques de Reiset, a French government official of the Restoration era.","Portrait of Madame Reiset"],"20268360":["The Revolt of Cairo is an 1810 history painting by the French artist Anne-Louis Girodet de Roussy-Trioson.","The Revolt of Cairo"],"20891091":["The Portrait of Mlle Lange as Danaë is a painting by French painter Anne-Louis Girodet de Roussy-Trioson.","Portrait of Mlle. Lange as Danae"],"29214871":["Hippocrates Refusing the Gifts of Artaxerxes is a 1792 history painting by the French artist Anne-Louis Girodet de Roussy-Trioson. It depicts a scene on the island of Kos in Ancient Greece.","Hippocrates Refusing the Gifts of Artaxerxes"],"29901380":["Portrait of Jean-Baptiste Belley is an oil on canvas portrait painting by the French artist Anne-Louis Girodet de Roussy-Trioson, from 1797. It depicts Jean-Baptiste Belley, a former slave from Saint-Domingue who was elected to serve in the National Convention following the French Revolution.","Portrait of Jean-Baptiste Belley"],"50350126":["Napoleon Receiving the Keys of Vienna is an oil on canvas history painting by the French artist Anne-Louis Girodet de Roussy-Trioson, from 1808.","Napoleon Receiving the Keys of Vienna"],"51578930":["Portrait of Chateaubriand is a c.1809 portrait painting by the French artist Anne-Louis Girodet de Roussy-Trioson. It depicts the French statesman and author François-René de Chateaubriand.","Portrait of Chateaubriand"],"59211717":["Portrait of Jacques Cathelineau is an 1816 oil painting by the French artist Girodet. Combining elements of history painting and portraiture it depicts Jacques Cathelineau one of the leaders of the War in the Vendée, a major but unsuccessful uprising against the French Revolution.","Portrait of Jacques Cathelineau"],"93456839":["Danaé is an oil painting by French artist Anne-Louis Girodet de Roussy-Trioson depicting the Greek princess Danaë being showered in gifts sent by Zeus.","Danaé"],"108686573":["Coriolanus Taking Leave of His Family is a 1786 history painting by the French artist Anne-Louis Girodet de Roussy-Trioson. It depicts a scene featuring the legendary Roman general Gnaeus Marcius Coriolanus departing from his grieving family, having been banished from the city.","Coriolanus Taking Leave of His Family"],"131742917":["The Death of Tatius is a 1788 history painting by the French artist Anne-Louis Girodet. Produced the year before the French Revolution, it is in the Neoclassical style.","The Death of Tatius"],"132674906":["Joseph Recognised by His Brothers is a 1789 history painting by the French artist Anne-Louis Girodet de Roussy-Trioson. It portrays the biblical story of Joseph who is recognised in Ancient Egypt by the brothers who had once sold him into slavery.","Joseph Recognised by His Brothers"]},"titlesFrom":["fr","P1476","alias:en","alias:fr","aliasFilter:1"]}